Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||11-09-2001||01:20 PM||||I've tried to do some searching but most of the searches indicates irregular idling.  When I start my car, it will always idle at 1,500 to 2,000.  But if I try to drive it immediately, it runs like CRAP.  It usually won't like to accelerate, but then a second or two later she'll burst ahead.  Then slow down and burst ahead again, back and forth.  Sometimes doing these cycles like 2 times per second.  It's pretty annoying.  But after 1 minute of warming up, she would then run smoothly.  But the weird thing is, it's not even cold at all outside, she would still run like crap when not running for half a day.  She runs like crap when I try to accelerate under 2,500 rpms.  Over that, she would then run smoother.  Shift to 2nd and it's crap again until I pass 2,500.  If I hold my clutch in, she would then run steadily somewhere between 1,500 and 2,000.  Nor rough, just steady.<P>It's apparently she doesn't want to run under load, before warm up.  When not under load, she runs pretty steadily.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">  </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||1
